  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Tuesday)\n\nLight isolated to scattered showers, as well as a few \nthunderstorms will continue tonight into Tuesday as a upper level \ntrough lifts across central and eastern Nevada. However there will\nbe a sharp cutoff in precipitation chances as locations east of a\nElko to Grass Valley, to Tonopah line will see a 30% to 70% \nchance for isolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms with \nsome locations seeing up to 0.40\u201d of precipitation. West of this \nline will see little in the way of moisture, with just increased \ncloud cover for Tuesday. The upper trough looks to shift east \nWednesday, as the upper pattern over the Silver State becomes weak\nas a very broad upper level troughing redevelops on the back side\nof the departing trough, over Nevada and most of central and \nsouthern California. This flow setup looks to last through Sunday \nas a northern stream system looks to reset the SW flow over the \nGreat Basin for Monday ahead of what may be a third upper level \ntrough passing through Nevada Monday and Tuesday. Models differ \nsome what on timing and position, as the GFS keeps the trough \nfaster and shallower pushing the main energy through the Pacific \nNW and into Wyoming by Monday morning While the ECMWF is slower, \nstronger and further south moving the trough over southern Nevada \nthrough Tuesday morning. Unfortunately, the one main issue that \nmodels agree on is that this series of troughs will have almost no\nmoisture to work with, keeping any precipitation out of the \npicture through next Wednesday at the least. The flip side is that\nwinds will be relatively light for the period with W-SW winds \nranging 5 MPH to 15 MPH with gusts up to 25 MPH possible. \nTemperatures will see a quick warm-up into the mid 80s by Thursday\nafternoon, before a cooling trend takes over due to a series of \ncool fronts associated with the upper troughing pattern drops \nhighs back into the .middle 70s. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence in a 30% to 70% chance for isolated to \nscattered showers and storms Tuesday for central and far eastern \nNevada.\n\nThere is high confidence in a much drier, yet cooler and less \nwindy pattern for Nevada starting Thursday.",
